Z||000000||Carolina 88GT||03-03-2000||06:50 PM||||Outta the shop and back on the road.  Took a couple days but......<UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI> New Exhaust, muffler, cat.<BR><LI> Accel Coil and Control Module<BR><LI> New Bosch Platinum +4 plugs<BR><LI> Rotor, distributor<BR><LI> Bosch o2 sensor<BR><LI> New MAP Sensor<BR><LI> On tuesday...New 160 deg. Thermostat and fan switch.<BR><LI> Also on tuesday, new IAC.<BR></UL><BR>Looking for some 8.8mm (or better) sparkplug wires.  Car is running sweet.  Will post a few pics and do some wavs.  And just to make myself feel better...went out and toasted an Accura Integra, some form of V8 Jeep, and a Berretta.  Anyone know of a good place for wires?  I dont want a "universal" style.||||reg||14
Z||000001||Oreif||03-04-2000||12:23 AM||||I know Pep Boys carries the Accel 8.8's that's where I got mine. So I take it it runs fine with the Bosch +4's? I tried Split-Fires once and they didn't work too well.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||03-04-2000||01:42 AM||||I put Bosch +4 in my GT last fall.   It made it run smoother.  I just put them in my Son's GT also.  I tried Split-Fires in my 67 Buick conv and my 90 Chev 4x4 pickup.  I didn't like Split-Fires at all.  Rough idle after a few thousand miles.||||reg||1
